        <h1 class="lt-h1">Why Parents Trust Muzzle Sleep: One of the Only Mouth Tapes Tested Across 500+ Chemicals</h1>

        <div class="lt-media">
          <img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0886/5542/9998/files/Frame_5_c4e6032e-c575-4cd2-abf0-6579e87e4f19.png" alt="Hero image placeholder">
        </div>

        <p class="lt-p">For adults looking to improve sleep, recovery, focus, and overall health, mouth taping shouldn’t come with chemical unknowns.</p>
        <p class="lt-p">You deserve a product that strengthens your sleep — not one that introduces questionable materials onto your skin for 7–9 hours each night.</p>
        <p class="lt-p">That’s why Muzzle Sleep was developed with a simple promise:</p>

        <div class="lt-highlight">Better sleep should never come with hidden ingredients.</div>

        <p class="lt-p">And to uphold that promise, we took an approach that’s almost unheard of in the consumer product space:</p>
        <p class="lt-p"><strong>We tested our <em>entire finished tape</em> across more than 500 chemicals,</strong> including some of the most advanced PFAS screenings available today.</p>
        <p class="lt-p">Here’s why clean-sleep enthusiasts, biohackers, and longevity-minded adults are switching to Muzzle.</p>

        <h2 class="lt-h2">Not Bamboo. Not Rayon. Not Plastic.</h2>

        <div class="lt-media lt-media-gap">
          <img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0886/5542/9998/files/Frame_5_1_19158396-6efa-418f-bc8b-c975db85a523.png" alt="Fabric illustration placeholder">
        </div>

        <p class="lt-p">A Clean, Breathable Fabric Backing — By Design.</p>
        <p class="lt-p">A growing number of mouth tape brands advertise their material as “bamboo,” “bamboo silk,” or “organic bamboo fiber.”</p>
        <p class="lt-p">But the truth is:</p>

        <!-- FIX: in design there are multiple highlight strips here -->
        <div class="lt-highlight">“Bamboo fabric” is almost always rayon (also called viscose).</div>
        <p class="lt-p">Rayon is a <strong>synthetic fiber</strong>, created by dissolving cellulose into a chemical soup and reforming it into threads.</p>
        <p class="lt-p">According to the U.S. Federal Trade Commission (FTC), bamboo textiles labeled simply as “bamboo” are typically:</p>
        <div class="lt-highlight diff-color">“Rayon made using toxic chemicals, not natural bamboo fiber.” — FTC Consumer Guidance</div>

        {% comment %} <p class="lt-p">Even the U.S. Federal Trade Commission warns consumers that textiles advertised as “bamboo” are typically chemically processed rayon, not natural bamboo fiber.</p> {% endcomment %}

        <p class="lt-p">The rayon-making process commonly uses:</p>
        <ul class="lt-list">
          <li><span class="lt-check" aria-hidden="true"><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0886/5542/9998/files/Vector.svg?v=1766611779"></span>Carbon disulfide</li>
          <li><span class="lt-check" aria-hidden="true"><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0886/5542/9998/files/Vector.svg?v=1766611779"></span>Sulfuric acid</li>
          <li><span class="lt-check" aria-hidden="true"><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0886/5542/9998/files/Vector.svg?v=1766611779"></span>Sodium hydroxide</li>
        </ul>        
        <p class="lt-p">Research published through Harvard-affiliated environmental health resources has highlighted that carbon disulfide exposure in production settings has been associated with neurological, cardiovascular, and reproductive effects in workers.</p>
        <p class="lt-p">To be clear:<br>We are not claiming any specific brand uses these chemicals — only that the rayon/bamboo viscose manufacturing process often does, as documented in textile science literature. And that's exactly why we rejected bamboo-rayon entirely.</p>
        <h2 class="lt-h2">Our Backing: A Simple, Clean, Breathable Cotton-Blend Fabric</h2>
        <div class="lt-media lt-media-gap">
          <img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0886/5542/9998/files/Frame_5_1_19158396-6efa-418f-bc8b-c975db85a523.png" alt="Fabric closeup placeholder">
        </div>
        <p class="lt-p">Instead of rayon, plastic films, or “eco-friendly” buzzwords, we use a soft, breathable textile made from:</p>
        <div class="lt-comp">
          <div class="lt-comp-inner">
              <img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0886/5542/9998/files/Frame_146_11269c4f-8687-412e-af88-2d1cfaae8d23.png" alt="Composition diagram placeholder (95% / 5%)">
          </div>
        </div>
        <ul class="lt-list">
          <li><span class="lt-check" aria-hidden="true"><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0886/5542/9998/files/Vector.svg?v=1766611779"></span>No bamboo rayon</li>
          <li><span class="lt-check" aria-hidden="true"><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0886/5542/9998/files/Vector.svg?v=1766611779"></span>No polyethylene or polypropylene film</li>
          <li><span class="lt-check" aria-hidden="true"><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0886/5542/9998/files/Vector.svg?v=1766611779"></span>No hidden plastic substrates</li>
          <li><span class="lt-check" aria-hidden="true"><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0886/5542/9998/files/Vector.svg?v=1766611779"></span>No chemical-intensive fiber processing</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="lt-p">Just clean, comfortable fabric that feels good on your skin.</p>

        <h2 class="lt-h2">Tested as a Complete Finished Product —<br>Not Just the Adhesive</h2>

        <p class="lt-p">We test the entire tape exactly as you use it — including:</p>

